# A stdlib-shaped generic holding a `T?`, instantiated over `string` from another module.
#
# `TypeLowering::optional_llvm_type` used to look its type up **by name**, so the second unit adopted the
# first one's `eco.optional.*` - whose payload slot is the *first* unit's `%string`, while every value that
# unit inserts is its own `%string.1`. IR verification failed with "Invalid InsertValueInst operands".
#
# It is per unit now, exactly like every other struct, which the structural ODR check is what makes safe.
modules: modules/lib_optpayload

